# Project-basic implementation record

## Delivered bounded change

This change adds the standalone data-only bundled pack `project-basic@0.1.0` without changing
FORGE's framework version (`1.0.0`), protocol version (`1.4.0`), core lifecycle services, CLI
default (`software-basic`), executable capabilities, or persisted authorization model.

The pack defines the fixed seven-phase workflow:

| Phase | Required outputs |
|---|---|
| `intake` | `human-vision-brief`, `owner-context-and-learning-profile` |
| `research` | `context-readiness-report`, `project-research` |
| `plan` | `project-plan`, `task-map`, `acceptance-criteria` |
| `create` | `created-work` |
| `evaluate` | `evaluation-report` |
| `review` | `review-report` |
| `close` | `lessons`, `closure-record` |

It has all four explanation profiles, four document-first interview guidance groups, and phase
guidance for every step. The guidance is digest-bound presentation text only: it cannot change
actors, conditions, transitions, verification, or owner acceptance. It describes small
beginner-friendly question batches, vision playback, known/uncertain/blocked status, workflow-fit
routing, practice versus review tasks, major-artifact review pauses, and bounded revocable
conversational authorization envelopes.

Research remains mandatory. The readiness template permits a documented no-new-research-needed
outcome only when it identifies the considered material, sufficiency basis, remaining uncertainty,
and owner review. The evaluation template names the exact created-work and acceptance-criteria
revision IDs and digests being assessed. Findings do not transition the workflow automatically.

Eleven declared read-only templates cover every role except domain-specific `created-work`.
Templates are list/show reference resources, not artifact generators or approvals. Native artifact
revision invalidates completed downstream work and supports the normal `rework` transition; no
mandatory `revise` phase was added.

